  level=logging.INFO,\n42:     format=\"%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s\"\n43: )\n44: logger = logging.getLogger(\"msemax.webhook\")\n45: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":7484,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T16:05:41Z","thinking":"Determining the number of existing completed model turns is the first step. The code attempts to directly count these turns within the webpage's content, using a selector to identify relevant elements. This count is stored in the `initial_model_count` variable.\n\n```\n\n\nInitial count of model turns is being determined by filtering elements based on attributes, classes, and inner text, primarily looking for indicators of model responses and thoughts within the webpage's structure. Error handling is included to catch and log any issues during this count inspection. The extracted turn count is then logged for tracking.\n\n\nInitial suspicion of a potential error triggered a search within the document for error indicators; this search revealed the presence or absence of an error. The program then evaluated if any chat turns exist in the document, and if so, it filters these turns to isolate model-generated responses. This count of model responses helps determine the agent's progress.\n\n\nIdentifying the most recent model turns is critical to understand the agent's recent activity. The code isolates these turns by iterating backward from the end of the chat history, stopping when a user turn is detected. The extracted turns are then reversed to maintain chronological order.\n\nThe content from each identified turn is extracted to build a consolidated text representing the agent's most recent reasoning steps. This process ensures only relevant information is captured.\n\n\nFiltering the extracted text is essential to exclude headers, buttons, and citations that are irrelevant to the core reasoning. Temporary concealment of these elements facilitates clean content extraction. Only the primary text content from each turn is preserved to build a comprehensive summary.\n\n\nState changes are now tracked, transitioning from a \"no response\" state to an \"in progress\" state upon detecting activity or if the process is running. A milestone indicating turn detection is recorded at this point. Timing metrics are extracted for analysis after completion, focusing on time to first token and total response time.\n\n\nVerification of JSON validity is being reviewed, specifically the logging of validation results. Examination of API endpoints reveals the extraction and forwarding of a batch size parameter to a core function. Further investigation focuses on a specific file, examining how it handles batch size within a function responsible for interacting with an external API.\n\n\nError handling is being implemented to address potential issues during data processing. Specifically, checks are in place to manage expired sessions, payload size limitations, and rate-limiting responses from the external resource. Adaptive splitting of data chunks is employed to handle large payloads, and exponential backoff is used for rate-limiting.  Failure to establish a connection is also being handled.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"D:/AI_Engineer/MSEMAX-GAIStudio/app.py\"","EndLine":"30","StartLine":"20","toolAction":"\"Viewing file\"","toolSummary":"\"View typing imports in app.py\""}}]}
